{"id": "EUVD-2026-82251", "enisaUuid": "8e5ce5da-e6f4-3733-b1ba-3d0f816c708f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: media: ipu7: fix pm_runtime refcount leak in ipu7_resume()\n\nipu7_resume() calls pm_runtime_get_sync() before resuming the device.\nIf the runtime PM resume fails, the usage count remains incremented, but\nthe error path returns without dropping the reference.\n\nUse pm_runtime_resume_and_get() instead, which balances the usage count\non failure and avoids the leak. Keep returning 0 on error, as resume\ncallbacks should not propagate failures to the PM core, matching the\nbehaviour of the ipu6 driver.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/593fda71983b9c23c84a566b20c53dc402c6b376", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/437d6d15936db87485afabf7d52754b7b19cc787", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b298b80814dd0fc3cb1c8c0e0082fc14fdb5fecf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f9hr-9g5j-m6mm", "CVE-2026-93143"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05059ddc-c93c-3b1a-b647-ef8da53e26c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7fe4c0019b12d60ece3e99eeb0ccfd5a1d103e5 <437d6d15936db87485afabf7d52754b7b19cc787"}, {"id": "2fb36431-3349-3b99-9bb3-7c28c5964f71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "3485c2f8-fba0-39b2-9e0f-214989c5f8ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6af851e5-87c1-3143-a3d2-a6b319b79e54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "78f4b5c1-ed71-3c52-afd1-791db4dda965", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "85416e92-6c14-3c4d-85c1-f5c3fab0da24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "d78d7ce2-8ab1-3d6f-941d-baf69fda8ac2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7fe4c0019b12d60ece3e99eeb0ccfd5a1d103e5 <b298b80814dd0fc3cb1c8c0e0082fc14fdb5fecf"}, {"id": "ee8b12fb-eea5-3268-9258-0c3d8354fc1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7fe4c0019b12d60ece3e99eeb0ccfd5a1d103e5 <593fda71983b9c23c84a566b20c53dc402c6b376"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5566c452-c83f-3fda-bfb3-f55ea1609750", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}